# Cloudflare Pages redirects (copied to the build root from public/).
# Path of Building's files are served at /pob-app/<build>/; the address people
# see and share is the app's /pob route (fullscreen) or /web-pob. Old links
# into /pob/ (the root, or a build folder) go to /pob; the browser keeps their
# #build= across the redirect.
/pob/*  /pob  302

# No /* /index.html 200 here: Pages follows _redirects even where a file
# exists, so a catch-all would shadow /pob-app/. The build has no top-level
# 404.html, so Pages already serves index.html for every path that is not a
# file (its single-page application mode). pob-app/404.html keeps missing PoB
# files a real 404 instead of the Angular page.
